  "term": "motor pathway",
  "definition": "In birdsong research, the motor pathway is the set of connected brain nuclei responsible for producing song by coordinating the muscle systems used for vocalization. In the source packet, this pathway includes HVC, the robust nucleus of the arcopallium, and the tracheosyringeal motor nucleus.",
